.TH V23-SECURITY 2
.SH NAME
V23security: Principal, Blessings, Caveat, createprincipal, blessself, bless, verifyblessings, pattern_match, authorize \- Vanadium principals and blessings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "sys.m";
include "keyring.m";
include "v23.m";
v23 := load V23security V23security->PATH;

Caveat: adt {
    id:     string;     # "const" | "expiry"
    param:  string;
};

Certificate: adt {
    extension:  string;
    pk:         ref Keyring->PK;
    pkstr:      string;
    caveats:    list of Caveat;
    sig:        ref Keyring->Certificate;
    sigstr:     string;
};

Blessings: adt {
    chains: list of list of ref Certificate;
    pk:     ref Keyring->PK;
};

Principal: adt {
    sk:     ref Keyring->SK;
    pk:     ref Keyring->PK;
    store:  list of ref StoreEntry;
    def:    ref Blessings;
    roots:  list of ref RootEntry;

    publickey:   fn(p: self ref Principal): ref Keyring->PK;
    blessself:   fn(p: self ref Principal, name: string,
                    cavs: list of Caveat): (ref Blessings, string);
    bless:       fn(p: self ref Principal, key: ref Keyring->PK,
                    with: ref Blessings, ext: string,
                    cavs: list of Caveat): (ref Blessings, string);
    sign:        fn(p: self ref Principal, msg: array of byte):
                    (ref Keyring->Certificate, string);
    setdefault:  fn(p: self ref Principal, b: ref Blessings): string;
    setdefaultnil: fn(p: self ref Principal);
    store_set:   fn(p: self ref Principal, b: ref Blessings,
                    pattern: string): string;
    forpeer:     fn(p: self ref Principal, peer: list of string):
                    ref Blessings;
    addroot:     fn(p: self ref Principal, b: ref Blessings): string;
    addrootkey:  fn(p: self ref Principal, pk: ref Keyring->PK,
                    pattern: string): string;
};

init:               fn(): string;
createprincipal:    fn(bits: int, owner: string): (ref Principal, string);
unconstrained:      fn(): Caveat;
expiry:             fn(until: int): Caveat;
blessingnames:      fn(b: ref Blessings): list of string;
encodeblessings:    fn(b: ref Blessings): string;
decodeblessings:    fn(s: string): (ref Blessings, string);
verifyblessings:    fn(p: ref Principal, b: ref Blessings):
                        (list of string, list of string);
pattern_valid:      fn(pat: string): int;
pattern_match:      fn(pat: string, names: list of string): int;
authorize:          fn(allow: list of string, remote: list of string): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B V23security
implements Vanadium-style principals and blessings on top of
.IR keyring-intro (2).
.B Init
must be called first; it returns nil on success or a diagnostic.
.PP
.B Createprincipal
generates an Elgamal key of
.I bits
bits (default 512 if
.I bits
≤ 0) owned by
.IR owner .
.SS Caveats
.B Unconstrained
returns a const caveat that always validates
.RB ( "const" / "true" ).
.B Expiry
returns a caveat that fails when
.IR daytime (2)
.B now
is after
.I until
(epoch seconds).
.B Bless
requires at least one caveat; use
.B unconstrained
for unrestricted delegation.
.SS Blessings
.B Blessself
creates a self-signed root blessing named
.IR name .
.B Bless
extends each chain in
.I with
by
.I ext
for
.IR key ;
.I with
must be bound to the local principal’s public key.
.PP
.B Blessingnames
returns claimed names (extensions joined by
.BR : ).
.B Verifyblessings
checks signatures, caveats, and whether chain roots are trusted via
.B addroot
/
.BR addrootkey ;
it returns
.BI ( recognized , rejected )
where rejected entries are
.BI name : reason
strings.
.PP
.B Encodeblessings
/
.B decodeblessings
use the framing in
.IR v23 (6).
Canonical
.B pkstr
/
.B sigstr
fields preserve Keyring text exactly for digest stability.
.SS Store and roots
.B Setdefault
sets blessings presented when acting as a server (or when no store entry matches).
.B Store_set
associates blessings with a peer blessing
.IR pattern .
.B Forpeer
selects store blessings for peer names, else the default.
.B Addroot
trusts the root public key of each chain in
.I b
for the claimed name pattern.
.SS Patterns and ACL
.B Pattern_match
implements Vanadium pattern rules
.RB ( ... ,
optional
.B :$
terminator, prefix match).
.B Authorize
returns nil if any
.I remote
name matches any pattern in
.IR allow ,
else a diagnostic.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/v23/security.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR v23-intro (2),
.IR v23-rpc (2),
.IR v23 (6),
.IR keyring-gensk (2),
.IR keyring-certtostr (2),
.IR daytime (2)
.SH BUGS
.IP \(bu
Only
.B const
and
.B expiry
caveats are implemented; unknown caveat ids fail verification.
.IP \(bu
.B PurposeDischarge
is defined but third-party caveats/discharges are not implemented.
.IP \(bu
Blessing store and roots are in-memory only; process exit loses them.
.IP \(bu
.B Forpeer
picks the matching store entry with the most chains, not Vanadium’s full
pattern-specificity rules.
.IP \(bu
Signature hashing uses SHA1 because
.IR keyring-intro (2)
.B sign
/
.B verify
accept only sha1/md5/md4 as the
.I ha
argument.
.IP \(bu
No x509-backed
.B BlessSelf
(Vanadium’s TLS certificate principals).
